Skip every drive root in a volume's mount point list in getmntent().
getmntent() lists drive letters first and then, for each volume, the
folders where it is mounted, skipping drive roots such as "D:\" that
it has already listed. After skipping one it used the next path
without checking it, so for a volume with two drive letters in a row
in its list, the second drive root was listed again as a mounted
folder, and df showed that drive twice. Keep skipping while the path
is a drive root.

---
 win32/mntent.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/win32/mntent.c
+++ b/win32/mntent.c
@@ -138,7 +138,7 @@
 	}
 
 	/* Skip mount points like 'C:/', we've already done them */
-	if (strlen(state->mount_ptr) == 3 &&
+	while (strlen(state->mount_ptr) == 3 &&
 			state->drives & 1 << (toupper(state->mount_ptr[0]) - 'A')) {
 		state->mount_ptr += 4;
 		if (state->mount_ptr[0] == '\0')
